request.intent:
`suggestSimilar(word, candidates)` currently only recognises an exact match, so a mistyped
command or flag produces no 'did you mean' hint. Implement real similarity matching in
`lib/suggestSimilar.js`.

Requirements:
- compare `word` against `candidates` using an edit distance that also counts a transposition of
  two adjacent characters as a single edit;
- only consider candidates within 3 edits, and reject any whose similarity, measured as
  (length - distance) / length against the longer of the two strings, is not greater than 0.4;
- candidates of one character or shorter are never suggested;
- keep only the closest candidates: a strictly better distance discards previous matches, an
  equal distance joins them;
- de-duplicate candidates, and sort the surviving suggestions with localeCompare;
- when `word` starts with '--', compare without the leading dashes but restore them in the output;
- return '' when nothing qualifies, '\n(Did you mean X?)' for one match, and
  '\n(Did you mean one of A, B?)' for several;
- return '' when candidates is empty, null or undefined.
